 r←Test_CheckVersions_061(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;dir;buff;rc;msg;filename;json
⍝ Run CheckForLaterVersion on an installed version that is ahead of everything the Registry hosts.\\
⍝ That is what a beta becomes once it has been published, installed, and then deleted again: the
⍝ Registry still knows the package name, so it answers with the best version of the major version
⍝ line - which is *older* than what is installed. Reporting that as an update, which comparing the
⍝ two IDs for being different rather than for being later once did, offers a downgrade.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 dir←∆GetTempDir''
 dir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣∆TEMP_TEST_DATA,'/myproj/*'

⍝ 1.99.0 is ahead of every 1.x the Registry has, and the Registry cannot be hosting it
 filename←dir,'/packages/',Reg.BuildListFilename
 json←⊃F.NGET filename
 json←'aplteam-versions-1.0.0-beta-1'⎕R'aplteam-versions-1.99.0'⊢json
 (⊂json)⎕NPUT filename 1

 buff←⎕FMT TC.CheckForLaterVersion dir,'/packages'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'<<< Not available any more >>>'⍷buff
 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/'1.0.0'⍷buff            ⍝ the earlier version the Registry offers must not be shown

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce dir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
